Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 49 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INTRADUCTAL  COMEDO  AND INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED NEAR BIOPSY CAVITY WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION THROUGHOUT THE BREAST AND METASTATIC TO SEVEN OF TWELVE AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Multiple microscopic foci of infiltrating ductal carcinoma are present in sections of breast taken away from the biopsy cavity  The resection margins are negative for carcinoma  however carcinoma is present near the deep resection margin  2  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH HEMORRHAGE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HEMOSIDERIN LADEN MACROPHAGES  AND FOAMY HISTIOCYTES  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 40                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  is a right modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring 30 x 20 x 5cm with an attached 13 x 8 x REMOVED_DATE axillary tail  An overlying 22 x 15cm ellipse of skin contains a slightly off center 4 5cm areola with a central grossly unremarkable 8mm nipple  In the upper quadrant in between the outer and inner quadrants is a well healed 4cm scar  3cm deep to this scar is a 3cm biopsy cavity filled with cloudy red fluid and lined by friable tan red tissue  The biopsy cavity is present 3cm from the deep margin  13cm from the inferior margin  5 5cm from the superior margin  13cm from the lateral margin  and 30cm from the axillary tail margin  Sectioning the remainder of the breast reveals grossly unremarkable mature adipose tissue with admixed fibrous bands  SECTION CODE  A  nipple and areola B  representative section of superior resection margin nearest biopsy cavity C  representative section of medial resection margin D  representative section of inferior resection margin E  representative section of deep resection margin  nearest biopsy cavity F  representative section of skin with scar  G K  representative section of biopsy cavity L O  representative section of remainder of breast P T  axillary lymph nodes ranging in size from 1mm to 1cm  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 09 41 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS on excisional biopsy  comedo type                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PREDOMINATELY GRADE 1 WITH FOCAL GRADE 2  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM AND LOCATED FAR AWAY FROM MARGINS  2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 15 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  3  ONE INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  4  COMPLEX SCLEROSING LESION  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  6  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The metastatic deposits in the lymph node aggregate to  0 1cm and consist of cohesive  whorled epithelial cell clusters located in the subcapsular sinuses  Their epithelial nature is confirmed by positive cytokeratin immunostaining  The slightly spindled morphology of the cells and the nuclear atypia are histologically similar to areas of the patient s ductal carcinoma in situ  Despite extensive examination and thorough sampling of the mastectomy specimen  no invasive carcinoma is found in the breast parenchyma itself  Review of the patient s prior biopsy specimens does not reveal any invasive component  Drs  Dennis Sgroi and Ben Pilch have reviewed selected slides and concur with the diagnosis of metastatic carcinoma  The ductal carcinoma in situ demonstrates a prominent spindle cell morphology in many areas  and there is also focal comedonecrosis  A Grimelius stain is negative for argyrophilic granules  Stains for ER  PR  and Her 2 neu will be attempted on the remaining lymph node tissue and will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 57                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block O   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  No tumor cells are seen in the section stained for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 26 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mastectomy specimen with an REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm tan pink nipple bearing skin ellipse and a 9 x 6 x 2cm axillary tail marked by a suture  On the tan pink skin surface there are two linear scars  one in the upper inner quadrant measuring 2 8cm in greatest dimension  and a second scar in the lower inner quadrant measuring 3 5cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two well healing biopsy cavities which are adjacent to each other  located in the medial aspect of the breast  The more medial of the cavities measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  The adjacent biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The cavities are surrounded by fat necrosis  The more medial of the cavities is 0 6cm to the closest posterior margin while the other cavity is 2cm to the closest posterior margin  The remainder of the breast is notable for diffuse thick fibrous tissue with numerous cysts ranging in size from 0 2cm to 1 4cm  Additionally there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm pink papillary nodule in the midline of the breast which is located 2cm from the closest posterior margin  The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes  which range in size from REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 9cm to 0 2cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE A B  Biopsy cavity  1  with closest posterior margin in A  C D  Biopsy cavity  2  E  Small papillary mass  F  Fibrocystic change from lower inner quadrant  G  Fibrocystic change and posterior margin from lower outer quadrant  H  Fibrocystic area from upper inner quadrant  I  Fibrocystic change from upper outer quadrant  J  Axillary lymph node  bisected and entirely submitted  K P  Axillary lymph nodes  entirely submitted  Q R  Representative sections of largest lymph node  S Z  Biopsy cavities  AA BB  Remainder of largest lymph node  CC    axillary lymph node  DD HH  Parenchyma JJ KK  Biopsy cavity LL  Parenchyma Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD Jonathan Michael Winograd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 15 55 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass  history of ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  80   FOCALLY PRESENT AT INKED SURGICAL MARGIN  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  20   WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite vascular invasion is present  The invasive carcinoma is present in four slides and is 1 4cm in greatest dimension  Results of staining for estrogen and progesterone receptor will follow in an addendum  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 15 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 14 56     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of soft  lobulated  yellow tissue with attached localizing wire and specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a firm  tan area  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  extending to an inked margin  Entirely submitted for permanents in A through G  A   section nearest to needle   Gross Description by  John Allick Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE O R  Resident  Jane M  Yang  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
