th red  The specimen is sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan firm nodule present focally at the superficial  anterior  resection margin  0 5cm from the medial margin and 1 0cm from the deep resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is fibrous and focally cystic  K  tumor with superficial and deep resection margins L M andN  tumor with deep resection margin O  fibrous area with superficial and superior resection margins Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superifical margin of breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of unoriented fibroadipose tissue which is inked and section  and submitted entirely in cassettes P and Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary tissue contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibroadipose tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes R and S  Received fresh  labeled  additional left axillary tissue  are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and each  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node  The fibroadipose tissue fragments are submitted entirely in cassette T  The lymph node is bivalved and submitted in cassette Q  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  TUMOR PRESENT AT A SUPERFICIAL  ANTERIOR  MARGIN  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT  PART C  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT  PART D  BREAST  LEFT SUPERFICIAL MARGIN  PART E  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
