Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA  Eighty five year old female with 2cm mass in left breast  FNA positive for cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY AND MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE WITH MUCIN PRODUCTION AND SIGNET RING CELLS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures approximately 2 5cm in greatest dimension  The inked resection margins are negative for carcinoma  There is no evidence of malignancy in 13 out of 13 lymph nodes  In areas the tumor has a colloid pattern  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  Virtually all of the tumor is infiltrating  however  there is one focus of severe ductal hyperplasia  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 15                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Estradiol receptor  Positive 66 femtomoles mg protein  Progestin receptor  Not determined  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 11     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY AND MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   6   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase rangi