Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 58 CLINICAL DATA  62 year old female with a positive breast biopsy for invasive ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  3 0CM  PRESENT ADJACENT TO THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Resection margins appear free of carcinoma  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion not seen  2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  16  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 34                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  labeled  left breast  only is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring 24 x 20 x 5 5cm with an associated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse with the nipple at the inferior of the skin ellipse  A 3 2cm  well healed scar is present in the upper inner quadrant  and an associated 0 3cm skin ulcer with white raised borders at one edge of the incision  Attached are the axillary contents which measure 13cm x 10cm x 2cm  There are no palpable masses  The specimen is inked and the axillary dissection is removed for an axillary dissection  and the nodes were submitted in A E  The mastectomy specimen is serially sectioned laterally to medially to reveal some firm  white breast tissue with grossly well defined borders that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  directly under the skin ellipse  Proceeding medially  there is a granular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE firm mass with poorly defined stellate borders present within 2 5cm of the medial margin  The closest margin deep  is approximately 0 5cm away from the mass and biopsy cavity  A E  axillary lymph nodes F  skin ulcer at incision G  scar H  mass adjacent to biopsy site I  biopsy cavity  deep margin J  additional section of mass  adjacent to biopsy cavity K  representative breast  large firm area  L  biopsy cavity  deep margin  superior portion M U  additional axillary lymph nodes Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST LEF   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 10 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT ON 9 OF 11 SLIDES AND EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE RESECTION MARGINS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 42 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm breast fragment  Inked and sectioned to reveal a tan firm cut surface  No frozen done  submitted entirely in A through K  Gross Description by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Resident  Frank P  Fechner  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
