skin ellipse oriented by a stitch in the axillary tail  The anterior surface is inked in blue and the posterior surface is inked in black  and the specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral  A poorly circumscribed irregularly shaped white to tan firm tumor is identified with areas of focal hemorrhage  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm and located 1 5cm to the closest anterior margin and 0 9cm to the closest posterior margin  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor to closest posterior black inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional tumor to black inked posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor to closest blue inked anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section of tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Normal tissue medial to tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Normal tissue lateral to tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Potential lymph node from axillary tail  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left sentinel node   is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of yellow tan fatty soft tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node which is bisected and a second possible REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm candidate node which is inked in black  Both are entirely frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART C  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only   report_end  , Unchecked.
