Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 91 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA  Previous biopsy of left breast showed lipoma  Probable carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  INVOLVING DERMIS   SEE NOTE  NOTE  No breast parenchyma is present  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The tumor is present at the surgical margins and involves most of the specimen  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 16 41                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative progesterone receptor  Not determined Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 AUG 91 at 16 32     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISION   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 309 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 5 6  and median of 4  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 12 00     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining of 100 breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 91 at 11 48     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The discrepancies between the results of immunohistochemical staining of paraffin sections  immunohistochemcical staining of frozen sections  and ligand binding assays probably result from technical difficulties with the latter two assays  The negative results probably represent falsely negative determinations  and it seems likely that the positive result obtained using paraffin sections represents the true situation  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 14 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 7cm  firm  white piece of fibroadipose tissue with an overlying tan  smooth  soft  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm skin ellipse with a central  1 4cm scar  The specimen is sectioned and reveals a dense  granular cut surface with white  firm  ill defined edges  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue is taken for BRDU and estrogen receptor studies  The remainder is submitted entirely in A  Resident  Dennis Sgroi  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH BREAST ORIGIN  O R  Resident  Erin L  McCann  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Edward Scully  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  OTTINGER LESLIE WAYNE PART   LEFT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
