esponding to the location of the wires  The first area of interest is an ill defined area of fibrous  rubbery breast parenchyma measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm that is located 0 5cm from the medial tip of the specimen and abuts the green  blue and black inked margins  The second area of interest is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3 cm firm  round  relatively well circumscribed  white to hemorrhagic area focally containing foreign material that is located 0 5cm from the nearest green inked margin  0 8cm to the nearest black inked margin  and 2 5cm from the lateral tip of the specimen  The third area of interest is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0 cm white  rubbery  fibrous  ill defined area of breast parenchyma that abuts the green  blue and black inked margins of the specimen and is located 1 0cm from the lateral tip  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  radially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  radially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First area of interest  calcification  medial   submitted from medial to lateral and including nearest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second area of interest  clip  middle   submitted from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Third area of interest  calcifications  lateral   submitted from medial to lateral  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY   NO CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY   report_end  , Unchecked.
