Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  26 AUG 97 at 13 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND TO SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  3  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  4  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion are not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 AUG 97 at 16 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that 