Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  18 AUG 97 at 12 52 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   95    REMOVED_DATE CM  GROSS MEASUREMENT   GRADE 2  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF A RESECTION MARGIN  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   5    LOW GRADE  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  MINOR FOCI ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND RARE MICROCALCIFICATIONS AWAY FROM THE MAIN TUMOR MASS  NOTE  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  20 AUG 97 at 16 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 97 at 08 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a 4 x 4 x 2 5cm piece of firm breast with localizing wire  The breast is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm firm  tan white  gritty mass with a stellate border  in areas coming to  0 5cm of the inked resection margin  Representative section of the mass are frozen as FX 1  other representative section are submitted through cassette A and G  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
