iochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are five parts  Labeled  right breast mass   is a 122 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The external surface is grossly unremarkable and inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a central gray white  firm to rubbery  centrally cystic mass REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  extending to within 0 4cm of an inked margin  The remaining breast tissue are strands of white pink fibrous septae in unremarkable yellow fibroadipose tissue  No other suspicious nodules are identified in the specimen  Representative sections of the tumor with margin are submitted in cassettes A through I  Representative sections of breast tissue are submitted in cassettes J through O  Labeled  right axillary lymph nodes  level 2   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue containing several rubbery nodules  in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Representative tissue is submitted in cassettes P through R  Labeled  axi