Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  HEMME  KELLIE     REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Specimen     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Clinical Information  LEFT BREAST 2 O  CLOCK 7 CM    Specimen s  Received  A  LEFT BREAST CORE BIOPSY      Diagnosis        FINAL REPORT          THIS REPORT IS AMENDED TO REPORT HER 2 neu STUDY BY FISH AND IHC  SEE  REPORT BELOW     LEFT BREAST CORE BIOPSY  2 O  CLOCK  7 CM    1  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES WITH  CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  NUCLEAR GRADE 3      NOTE  Invasive carcinoma involves all tissue fragments and measures up to  1 2cm in greatest linear extent     ESTROGEN PROGESTERONE RECEPTORS BY IMMUNOPEROXIDASE METHOD     ANALYSIS  MANUAL     RESULTS  ER    of tumor cells staining positively     95    PR    of tumor cells staining positively     80   See comment       INTERPRETATION    5  cells staining   favorable  1 4  cells staining   borderline   0  of cells staining   unfavorable    Immunostains are performed on formalin fixed paraffin embedded sections  using Ventana ER antibody clone  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and PR antibody clone 1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the  iVIEW  DAB polymer detection kit       Some investigators have reported that patients with as low as 1   positivity for ER PR may still respond to hormonal therapy     COMMENT  The ER PR immunostains were performed at NSMC and interpreted by  Dr  Linnea Garcia  These tests were developed and their performance  characteristics were determined by NSMC  They may not have been cleared or  approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  but the FDA has  determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  The tests are  for clinical purposes and should not be regarded as investigational  NSMC  laboratory is accredited by the College of American Pathologists  and is  approved by CLIA for the performance of high complexity testing       Fluorescence in situ Hybridization  FISH  Report  HER 2 neu    Result  AMPLIFIED  The Her 2 cen 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE    Specimen Site Type  Left Breast Core Tissue    Indication for Study  Evaluate for Her 2 neu Gene Amplification    The average of Her 2 neu copies per tile  REMOVED_DATE    The average of cen17 copies per tile  REMOVED_DATE    The cutoff point for assessing Her 2 neu gene amplification is a  Her 2 cen17 ratio greater than REMOVED_DATE    The specimen is considered AMPLIFIED for the Her 2 neu gene     A total of 179 tiles from this patient s tissue were analyzed by the Vysis  AutoVysion System and were sufficient for analysis     This patient specimen resulted in a Her 2 cen17 value of REMOVED_DATE and is  therefore considered amplified for the HER 2 gene  The  average HER 2 copy number was REMOVED_DATE copies per tile  Although the  biological and clinical basis for gene amplification is not  clear  it has been observed that the most aggressive disease stage is  associated with the highest frequency of gene  amplification  The HER 2 status of a tumor is a critical determinant of  response to trastuzumab based treatment  Benefit  correlates best with tumors that are determined to be amplified by  fluorescence in situ hybridization for HER 2  Clinical  correlation is advised     FISH was performed using the PathVysionHER 2 DNA Probe Kit     Probe Name Detection Parameters Result ISCN    PathVysion amplification of the HER 2 gene AMPLIFIED nuc  ish  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID x3  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID x14     Electronically Signed by Galina Bannykh  M D on REMOVED_DATE at US LABS    Methodology and Intended Use  Please see US Labs report     Disclaimer  This Test was performed at  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Campus Drive  Irvine  CA   REMOVED_CASE_ID     The PathVysion HER 2 DNA Probe Kit has been approved by the U S  Food    Drug Administration  FDA  for detecting amplification of the HER 2 neu gene  via fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  in formalin fixed   paraffin embedded human breast cancer tissue specimens  The performance  characteristics of this test have been established by US Labs       Predictive Prognostic Marker Analysis    Specimen Site  Lt Breast Specimen ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Dako HercepTest   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     IHC Reference Range  Equivocal Not Over Expressed 0   1   Score  2  Equivocal 2   Analysis  Manual Over Expressed 3     Electronically Signed by Galina Bannykh  M D on REMOVED_DATE at US LABS      Methodology and Intended Use  Please see US Labs report     Disclaimer  This Test was performed at  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Campus Drive  Irvine  CA   REMOVED_CASE_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  testing at US LABS is performed in compliance with standards set by  the  REMOVED_CASE_ID  ASCO CAP guidelines  If the result is EQUIVOCAL   2   comparison  with results from another methodology  such as FISH  may be of benefit    Wolff et al  ASCO CAP guideline recommendations for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  testing in breast  cancer  Arch Pathol lab Med   REMOVED_CASE_ID  131 18 43      ASCO CAP guidelines recommend fixation in neutral buffered formalin for a  minimum of 6 hours and a maximum of 48 hours  This is not an absolute  exclusion criterion  If the result is NEGATIVE  0 or  1  for specimens  fixed longer than 48 hours  the report should qualify that prolonged  fixation could be a possible cause  and the specimen should be tested by  FISH     Result Category IHC Score Interpretation Criteria    Positive 3  Strong  complete  homogeneous membrane  staining in  30  of cells     Equivocal 2  Strong  complete membrane staining in    30   of cells  Weak or moderate heterogeneous  complete membrane staining in at least 10  of cells   Negative 0 1  No staining  0   or weak  incomplete membrane  staining  1   in any percentage of cells     Linnea Garcia  M D   5 5 10  5 6 10  5 10 10           Electronically Signed Out 