Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 49 CLINICAL DATA  57 year old with palpable mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF CLOSEST INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    SOLID TYPE  PRESENT ADJACENT TO INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  NOTE  No definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast fragment with ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm white  firm lesion  less than 0 1cm from inked margin  The lesion is submitted in cassette A and B and the remainder of the specimen entirely in cassettes D L  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  SMALL HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS LESION  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
