he invasive nature  The invasive carcinoma appears to be of high grade  however  the very small size may limit accurate grading  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast needle loc   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm excisional breast specimen  The surgeon orients the lateral margin with a long stitch and the superior margin with a short stitch  The long axis of the specimen is in the anterior to posterior axis  The specimen is inked as follows  superior blue  inferior black  lateral yellow  medial green  Two localization wires are in place  one of which is an area  which abuts the anterior resection margin of the specimen  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm area of gray discoloration in this area located in the anterior inferior portion of the specimen  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow tan and without nodules or masses and with areas of white fibrous tissue  The following cassettes are submitted such that the specimen is entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial sections through anterior resection margin with described lesion particularly in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Serial sectioning from anterior to posterior with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  being most posterior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is the en face posterior resection margin  The second reported lesion from the radiograph is most likely in the cassette in or near  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See Note  Note  The tumor cells are very scant  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  FEW NESTS ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN TWO OF NINE LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY FAT  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 09                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a right modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a 19 x 17 x 5cm right breast  with an 8 x 6 x 3cm attached axillary tail  There is a central  overlying  19 x 8 5cm  tan ellipse of skin with an unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is a central  linear  healing  4 5cm scar  which is 1 0cm inferolateral to the nipple  Note that there are two eccentric ecchymoses  REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  1 3cm superomedial to the nipple  and REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  which abuts the inferior skin margin  Sectioning beneath the scar reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  diffusely hemorrhagic biopsy cavity which comes within  0 1cm of the deep resection margin  the closest margin   The biopsy cavity comes within 3cm of the superior margin  6cm of the inferior margin  and 3 5cm from the medial margin  The tissue surrounding the biopsy site is diffusely indurated  with focal  bright yellow changes in the adipose tissue  Focally  around the biopsy cavity  there are dense areas of fibrous tissue  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable  Dissection through the axillary tail reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging from 0 3cm in greatest dimension up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Section code  A B  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest deep margin C  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest overlying skin D E  Biopsy cavity with surrounded  indurated tissue F  Firm focus of fibrous tissue adjacent to biopsy cavity G I  Representative of each lymph node  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
