cm in diameter with inverted nipple and 2 5cm curvilinear scar in the superior medial aspect of the areolar  skin border  A long suture designates the lateral aspect and a short suture designates the superior aspect of the specimen  The external surface is lobulated  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a white  stellate  gritty area beneath the nipple areolar complex running into rubbery  white pink breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in greatest dimension and extending to 3 5cm of the deep margin  No biopsy cavity is identified  however  a bright yellow  gritty material surrounding this area suggesting a biopsy site  Multiple other foci of fibrous  white pink breast tissue without specific nodules are present throughout the specimen  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  the largest REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  SECTION CODE  A C  representative sections of the white  gray  stellate area under the areola  D F  representative adjacent breast tissue  G K  representative sections of the deep margin  L P  representative sections of breast tissue from medial to lateral  Q T  axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  Right axillary tissue   is a fragment of fibroadipose tissue containing a lymph node  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The lymph node is sectioned and submitted in cassette U  The remaining fibroadipose tissue is submitted in cassette V  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  SOFT TISSUE  RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 07 CLINICAL DATA  Status post needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   1    REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED   SEE NOTE   2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA   99    EXTENSIVE  MIXED COMEDO  MICROPAPILLARY  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES WITH FOCAL NEUROENDOCRINE FEATURES  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   3  RADIAL SCAR  MICROSCOPIC  NOTE  A single microscopic focus of infiltrating ductal carcinoma is seen in slide H  Due to the microscopic size of the invasive carcinoma  accurate grading of the tumor is not possible  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Intraductal carcinoma is present in seven of nine slides and spares at least 2 0cm  Microcalcifications are associated with the intraductal carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 40                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE IN SITU TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE IN SITU TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive tumor cells  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm fragment of breast tissue with localizing wire in place  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in cassettes A through I  Gross Description by  KEITH KWAN  MD Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   NO GROSS EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Chin lee Wu  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Adriana Dionigi Corben  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Bilateral simple mastectomies  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   2  FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA AND ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  SMALL INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITES  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  2  FIBROCYSTIC AND FIBROADENOMATOUS CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  SKIN TAG OF THE NIPPLE  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME     REMOVED_DATE  Received fresh  labeled with  left breast  stitch at 6 o clock   is a 25 x 20 x 2 5cm oriented left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 6 o clock  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nipple  which are both grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial lateral axis to reveal two biopsy sites  The first REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan white biopsy site lies approximately in the central quadrant of the breast  is associated with a metallic clip  and is located 5 5cm from the closest posterior margin and 2 5cm from the closest anterior margin  Approximately 5cm lateral to this  is the second REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white biopsy site  which is located in the outer quadrant of the breast  0 3cm from closest posterior margin and 1cm from the closest anterior margin  The breast parenchyma between the 2 biopsy sites has a tan yellow lobulated unremarkable cut surface  The remaining parenchyma of the specimen contains tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with no discrete mass or lesion  The upper outer quadrant tissue is also palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First biopsy site  entirely submitted  with closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second biopsy site  entirely submitted  with closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma between the 2 biopsy sites   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma of the upper inner quadrant  Received fresh  labeled with  right breast  stitch at 12 o clock   is a 26 x 21 x 3 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 12 o clock  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm unremarkable areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm nipple  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan brown papilliferous skin nodule  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial lateral axis to reveal a predominantly tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with a moderate amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  No discrete mass or lesion is noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is also palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections of the breast parenchyma are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the