h needle localization   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 2cm oriented breast tissue with 2 needle localization wires in place and short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The long axis of the specimen is superior to inferior  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  medial   green  and lateral   yellow  On sectioning  the breast parenchyma shows an irregularly outlined  tan pink to gray white  firm to hard tumor measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm and located 1 0cm from the nearest anterior margin and 2 0cm from the nearest posterior margin  The remaining resection margins are  1 0cm from the tumor  The remaining breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and pink white fibrous stroma  The tumor is located between the 2 needle localization wires  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior end margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor with anterior and posterior resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast  not involved by tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior end margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary contents   is a 12 x 10 x 2cm aggregate of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue  from which 14 lymph nodes are dissected  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The larger lymph nodes are bisected to reveal a tan white  firm to hard cut surface  grossly consistent with a metastatic deposit  The lymph nodes are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single whole lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single possible whole lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  