Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 32 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   LUMP    INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  FORMING MANY DISCRETE NODULES AS LARGE AS REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  INVOLVING MUCH OF THE SPECIMEN  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVELY INVOLVING THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  2   MASS    INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  2   MASS    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast tissue which is incised and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 3cm area of firm white tan poorly defined tissue  which is too small to freeze  This area was adjacent to the wire corresponding to calcifications  The firm area is in cassettes A through D  The remainder is in cassettes E through I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm tan stellate area extending to margin  Tissue submitted entirely in J through M  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST LUMP   ONE FIVE MILLIMETER AREA OF INDURATION  TO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY  SPCIMEN  1   LUMP  PART B  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY  SPCIMEN  2   MASS    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 54 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma with lumpectomy 7 years ago                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is very poorly circumscribed and is REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in cross section  as measured from the slides  It focally extends to within less than 1mm of the resection margin in several foci  A circumscribed nodule of tumor associated with a small rim of lymphocytes is also present  It is not possible to determine if this is a separate tumor nodule  or a small lymph node completely replaced by carcinoma  Extensive lymphatic permeation is present  There is no evidence of an in situ component  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 49                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 02     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  white  well defined 0 6cm nodule  adjacent to a firm  white  0 6cm poorly defined extending to within 0 1cm of the inked margin  A representative section from the area close to the margin is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  A thin sliver sent for BRDU  Lesion submitted in A F  Additional tissue submitted as G and H  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Li